---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Over-Terrain Vehicle" description="Magnetic detection subsystem for an autonomous over-terrain vehicle." currentPage="/projects">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="hero__eyebrow">Course Project · ENES100</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">Over-Terrain Vehicle</h1>
      <p class="hero__subtitle">
        Designed the magnetic-puck detection subsystem — from Faraday induction modeling
        to Hall-effect sensor implementation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="card fade-in" style="border-left:4px solid var(--accent); margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
        <p style="margin-bottom:0.25rem;"><strong>Course:</strong> ENES100 — Introduction to Engineering Design</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0.25rem;"><strong>Team project</strong></p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0;"><strong>My role:</strong> Magnetic detection subsystem design and electronics</p>
      </div>

      <div class="placeholder fade-in" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
        <!-- Replace with: OTV photo or circuit diagram -->
        <span>Vehicle photo or detection circuit diagram (800×400)</span>
      </div>

      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2>Problem</h2>
        <p>
          Build an autonomous vehicle capable of navigating over rough terrain and detecting
          a hidden magnetic puck. The detection subsystem needed to reliably identify the
          puck's location as the vehicle traversed the course.
        </p>

        <h2>Approach</h2>
        <p>
          I initially modeled a <strong>Faraday induction coil</strong> approach, analyzing
          the induced EMF as the vehicle passed over the magnetic puck. After evaluating
          signal-to-noise characteristics, I pivoted to a <strong>Hall-effect sensor</strong>
          for more reliable detection at the speeds and distances involved.
        </p>
        <p>
          I co-wired the Arduino electronics, integrating the Hall-effect sensor with the
          vehicle's main control board and writing the detection threshold logic.
        </p>

        <h2>Tools</h2>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:0.5rem; margin-top:0.5rem;">
          <span class="card__tag">Arduino</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Hall-Effect Sensor</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Electronics</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Breadboarding</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top:3rem;">
        <a href="/projects" class="btn btn--outline">← All Projects</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
